## C. The library field, sorted by the only axis that matters

**`*` The classification.** A rasteriser paints text into a bitmap and must then rebuild caret, selection, IME and the a11y tree. Several libraries **document this as the expected pattern**, which is the strongest possible self-conviction.

### (ii) DOM-hosting — the family we need

| | Licence | Alive? | Note |
|---|---|---|---|
| **xyflow** (React/Svelte Flow) | **MIT**, clean | **12.11.6 / 1.6.6 both 2026-09-01**; 10–50 commits/wk, no gaps; merged daily by Moritz Klack & Peter Kogo; xyflow GmbH, self-funded on Pro, no VC | **Clears both bars.** See below. |
| **tldraw** | proprietary | v5.4.0 today | Right family, licence fatal |
| **folkjs** | **MIT** | last commit 2026-05-19, ~16 zero weeks | Right *thesis*, unpublished, cooling |
| **JointJS core** | MPL-2.0 (verified raw) | `@joint/react@4.3.5`, 2026-08-24, 82 commits/26wk | Real `foreignObject` HTML host (`html-host.tsx`). File-level copyleft. |
| **AntV X6** | MIT, 6.7k★ | **12 commits in 26 weeks** | Slowing markedly |
| **LogicFlow** (didi) | Apache-2.0, 11.7k★ | 98 commits/26wk | Healthier than X6; Chinese-first docs |
| **BlockSuite** | MPL-2.0 | **zero commits in 26wk**; folded into AFFiNE monorepo (NOASSERTION) | Native web components **over Yjs** — architecturally our closest analogue. Clean library frozen, live code murkier licence. |
| **maxGraph** | Apache-2.0 | v0.24.0 2026-07-08, 52 commits/26wk | Quiet but genuinely alive |
| **rete.js** | MIT | core **zero commits in 26wk** | Right shape, wrong health |
| **daybrush stack** (`infinite-viewer`, `moveable`) | MIT | **zero commits in 52wk**, last release 2023 | **Dead.** This *was* the practitioner's stack. |
| **Kinopio** | **PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0** | pushed 2026-09-02, Vue 3 + DOM, indie | `!` I read the LICENSE.md — noncommercial-only. Beautiful indie prior art, licence-encumbered. |
| **dgmjs** | **GPL-3.0** | last push 2025-12 | Licence trap |

### Pan/zoom substrates — pure camera controllers, zero store, zero CRDT friction

`@panzoom/panzoom` (MIT, 4.6.2, **pushed today**) · `react-zoom-pan-pinch` (MIT, **4.1.1 shipped 2026-09-02**) · `d3-zoom` (ISC, feature-complete since 2021) · anvaka/panzoom (MIT, but 52wk participation nearly all zeros, 181 open issues, solo) · Leaflet with `CRS.Simple` + `L.DivIcon` genuinely works as a DOM substrate (BSD-2, but **no stable npm release in 3+ years**) · OpenSeadragon (BSD-3, 6.1.0 2026-08-06, active — but designed for a handful of annotation pins; `0` whether its overlay repositioning is transform-smooth is **unconfirmed, no source found**).

**`!` The rot to know about: `@use-gesture` last published 2024-03-21, last pushed 2024-07-15 — two years silent.** The animation half of the pmndrs stack (react-spring, motion) is thriving; the *gesture-recognition* half is not. If you reach for that stack, that is your single point of failure.

### (i) Rasterisers — disqualified, several by their own documentation

- **Excalidraw** — MIT, no watermark, 131k★, pushed 2026-09-01, David Luzar merges nearly everything; monetises via Excalidraw+ SaaS and Open Collective (**`0` no VC round found — no source found**). Disqualified on mechanism: `textWysiwyg.tsx` floats a real contenteditable over the canvas *while you type*, then **rasterises the text on blur**. Only its iframe "embeddable" hosts persistent live content. **`!` `excalidraw-room` last pushed 2024-07-12 — two years dormant; do not plan on it as a relay.**
- **Konva** — MIT, 10.3.2 (2026-08-26), effectively solo (Anton Lavrenov). Its own docs: *"Users cannot edit Konva.Text content directly for many reasons. The Canvas API is not designed for text editing"* — then prescribe hand-positioning a `<textarea>` per field. Our use case, disclaimed by the vendor.
- **Fabric.js v7** — MIT, v7.4.0 2026-05-18, thin cadence, one maintainer. `IText` paints its **own** cursor and selection rectangle from internal offsets, keystrokes via a hidden proxy input. Not browser selection. No arbitrary-DOM mechanism at all.
- **PixiJS v8** — MIT, v8.20.1 2026-08-26, company-backed. Most thoroughly disqualified: `Text` and `HTMLText` both terminate in a **texture**, and the new `pixi.js/html-source` (v8.19.0) captures live DOM **as a texture source** — the precise inverse of what we need.
- **CanvasKit / Skia** — BSD-3, `canvaskit-wasm` 0.42.0 2026-08-18, actively released by Google. Ships its own text-shaping stack (SkParagraph). Definitionally the wrong family — this is the thing your Flutter measurements measured. `skia-canvas` is a **Node native addon with no browser build**; server-side export only.
- **Motion Canvas** — MIT, **~1 commit in 52 weeks**, npm stuck at 3.17.2 (2024-12-14), sole author, 19k★, 173 open issues. Also a *video authoring* tool. Doubly out.
- **litegraph.js** — original last commit 2024-01-08; the lively `Comfy-Org` fork is **archived and declared end-of-life**, folded into ComfyUI_frontend under GPL-3.0. Dead upstream, licence dead end downstream.
- **Paper.js** — MIT by file text, **zero commits in 52wk**, 429 open issues. Dead.
- **jsPlumb** — Community hasn't published since 2021-05-27. The **Toolkit is proprietary with a confidentiality clause** ("treat the Source Code as secret and confidential") and the vendor says jsPlumb is in maintenance mode, sold only as renewals. **Avoid.**
- Cytoscape.js, sigma.js, deck.gl, Two.js, Rough.js — all raster or shape-only. `graphology` (MIT, pushed today) is a **pure data structure with no renderer** and can sit beside Automerge harmlessly.

### The two to keep regardless

**perfect-freehand** (MIT, Stephen Ruiz Ltd, 1.2.3 published 2026-02-01) and **Rough.js** (MIT, frozen 2023-11 but stable). Both are **stateless geometry helpers with no renderer and no DOM ownership** — points in, outline out. Automerge can own their input points directly. `!` These are the only two items on the original list that are unambiguously compatible with our architecture with no caveat.

`?` Note the pleasing symmetry: perfect-freehand is Steve Ruiz's, MIT, and unencumbered. We can take his ink without taking his licence.

